@startuml
title Album import: conceptual execution of coroutine stages
actor User
participant "CLI / TerminalImportSession" as CLI
participant "ImportSession" as Session
participant "Pipeline + beets.importer.stages" as Stages
participant ImportTask as Task
participant "beets.autotag" as Autotag
participant "beets.metadata_plugins / loaded providers" as Providers
participant Library
participant "Item / filesystem" as Files
participant "beets.plugins" as Plugins
User -> CLI : beet import
CLI -> Session : run()
Session -> Stages : build stages; run sequentially or in parallel
Stages -> Task : factory.tasks(): read items / create task
alt autotag enabled
  Stages -> Task : lookup_candidates(search_ids)
  Task -> Autotag : tag_album(source)
  Autotag -> Providers : candidates / albums_for_ids
  Providers --> Autotag : AlbumInfo / TrackInfo values
  Autotag --> Task : Proposal(candidates, recommendation)
  Stages -> Task : choose_match(session)
  Task -> CLI : choose_match(task)
  CLI --> Task : AlbumMatch or Action
else import as-is
  Stages -> Task : set_choice(Action.ASIS)
end
Stages -> Library : resolve duplicates through task operations
Stages -> Task : _apply_choice: apply_metadata() if selected
Stages -> Task : add(lib)
Task -> Library : add_album(items) / add or store items
Stages -> Task : set_fields(lib) if configured
Stages -> Plugins : early_import_stages and import_stages callbacks
Stages -> Task : manipulate_files(...)
Task -> Files : configured tag writing / file operations
Stages -> Task : finalize(session)
Task -> Plugins : album_imported event
note over Stages, Plugins
Events also occur during task creation, lookup, choice and file handling.
Skip, singleton, pretend, merge, rescan and reimport branches are omitted.
The diagram summarizes stage execution rather than every call frame.
end note
@enduml
